sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-cooke-clock-and-wavefront> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-cooke-clock-and-wavefront-overall> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-cooke-clock-and-wavefront-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Cooke & Zeeman (1976) clock-and-wavefront somite segmentation — MorphoEval overall 90.3/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Pass 3 post-remediation evaluation of `1976-cooke-clock-and-wavefront.py` (90.3/100, essentially flat vs 90.4 in Pass 2). Both Pass 2 remediation items are closed: (i) a reduced Goldbeter-Gonze-Pourquie (2007) FGF8/RA toggle driven by Dubrulle & Pourquie (2004) fgf8 mRNA decay behind an elongating tailbud now supplies the cusp unfolding parameter and commitment mobility, so the wavefront velocity is derived rather than prescribed (v_front = 2.22222 vs v_tb = 2.2222 um/min, S = 100.13 um, N = 40; S tracks v_tb*T_c across a 4-point sweep with RMSE 0.09 um; an FGF8 bead yields 0.70x smaller adjacent somites as in Dubrulle 2001); (ii) a Farhadifar (2007) vertex-model sheet of 360 PSM cells coupled through an anterior/posterior half-somite cleft rule forms 12 blocks at 100.0 um pitch and rotates the lattice cleft from 28.2 to 10.3 deg from the mediolateral axis (dLambda = 0 control 27.3 deg; SEM specimen clefts 7.9 deg) while straightening it (tortuosity 1.30 -> 1.03). Five new Lean 4 theorems (0 sorry) formalise the front-velocity and cleft-count laws. The score does not rise because the remediation exposed the next layer: the toggle is a two-variable reduction with tuned rather than published constants, the specimen has no um scale, the bead comparison is directional only, the sheet has no T1 transitions or rosettes, and the new reference JSON is recorded but not SHA-256-pinned. Overall 90.3/100 (faithfulness 89.7, reproducibility 91.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 91, Morphological realism / specimen match 87, Parameter expressivity 92, Morphometric validation 91, Source and data traceability 93, Code-to-model traceability 91, Reproducibility package 91. Output judged: docs/media/clock_and_wavefront_comparison.png: rendered output of 1976-cooke-clock-and-wavefront.py at d58a084, image/png, 1415556 B, 2310×2044 px, artifact_sha256 0a6c41da9df6f972bcba0ce2571dcdaa3d70ec1a69a8067f3c712f3fcb054a1c (sha256 0a6c41da9df6f972bcba0ce2571dcdaa3d70ec1a69a8067f3c712f3fcb054a1c), spec_fingerprint c943fd8ec360d2fc8a2730571fb91c8337ae0de4cb262a0f6d695d053bbbcf13. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: c943fd8ec360d2fc8a2730571fb91c8337ae0de4cb262a0f6d695d053bbbcf13; artifact_sha256: 0a6c41da9df6f972bcba0ce2571dcdaa3d70ec1a69a8067f3c712f3fcb054a1c; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/clock_and_wavefront/clock_and_wavefront_reference.json=4851550f4179ae63..., datasets/clock_and_wavefront/fgf_ra_vertex_reference.json=1dedf71c930b5ed0..., datasets/clock_and_wavefront/scout_manifest.json=0beabd3277c705e6..., datasets/clock_and_wavefront/somite_embryo_specimen.jpg=8b80971796cb29e2...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-clock-and-wavefront-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Cooke & Zeeman (1976) J. Theor. Biol. 58:455-476 kinematic somite wavelength law S = v * T_c and Thom-Zeeman cusp catastrophe wavefront manifold | Cooke (1975) Nature 254:196-199 Xenopus laevis blastula size-reduction invariance (N ~ 40 somites across normal and miniature embryos) | Goldbeter, Gonze & Pourquie (2007) Dev. Dyn. 236:1495-1508: mutual FGF/RA inhibition is bistable and its switching threshold defines a sharp determination front that moves with axis elongation; Dubrulle & Pourquie (2004) Nature 427:419-422: the fgf8 gradient is set by mRNA decay in cells leaving the tailbud | Dubrulle, McGrew & Pourquie (2001) Cell 106:219-232: an ectopic FGF8 bead produces smaller somites at its level (no numerical ratio reported) | Farhadifar et al. (2007) Curr. Biol. 17:2095-2104 vertex-model energy and case-I parameters; Bi et al. (2015) Nat. Phys. 11:1074-1079 shape-index rigidity transition p0* = 3.81; reconstructed_in_script: 1D anteroposterior Thom-Zeeman cusp catastrophe ODE tau_chi*dchi/dt = -(chi^3 - a(x,t)*chi - b_osc(x,t)) with either the prescribed kinematic front a = tanh((v t - x)/sigma_w) or the Goldbeter FGF/RA toggle front a = tanh((R - F)/kappa_a), m = F^4/(F^4 + K_mob^4), driven by tailbud elongation through M_F = exp(-(x_tb - x)/lambda_F), lambda_F = v_tb/k_dM (reduced two-variable toggle; Cyp26/Raldh2 lumped) | Endogenous front velocity fit (v_front = 2.22222 um/min vs v_tb = 2.2222, R^2 = 1.000), 4-point v_tb sweep (S RMSE 0.09 um), decaying-Gaussian FGF8 bead perturbation (min adjacent somite ratio 0.70, max 1.55) | Farhadifar vertex model of a 60 x 6 hexagonal PSM sheet (20 um pitch, Lambda_0 = 0.12, Gamma = 0.04, dLambda_cleft = 0.9, outer boundary pinned, gradient descent, no T1) in which only posterior(-1)->anterior(+1) half-somite interfaces are loaded: 12 clefts at 100.0 um pitch, cleft angle 28.2 -> 10.3 deg (control 27.3), tortuosity 1.30 -> 1.03, shape index 3.76 | Bilateral dorsal somite row DoG peak and inter-somitic cleft segmentation on somite_embryo_specimen.jpg (48.47 px mean spacing, symmetry ratio 0.9605) plus a per-cleft luminance-minimum line fit giving an empirical cleft angle of 7.9 deg; transfer_boundary: 1D anteroposterior paraxial mesoderm axis mapped to dorsal vertebrate SEM somite rows; the specimen is a chick SEM in pixels with no scale bar, so S_obs (px) is compared to the Cooke-Zeeman waveform shape and cleft orientation only, not to S_sim in um | The FGF/RA toggle parameters (alpha = 3, K = 1, n = 4, tau_FR = 12 min, k_dM = 0.0074/min) are tuned to place the front offset ~0.19 mm behind the tailbud; they are not Goldbeter et al.'s published kinetic constants, so only the qualitative predictions (bistability, v_front = v_tb, bead effect) are tested | The chi = +1 / -1 compartments of the cusp are read as anterior / posterior half-somites (Saga & Takeda 2001) to decide which interfaces are clefts; Cooke & Zeeman themselves did not make this identification; does_not_claim: The published 3-4 variable Goldbeter (2007) kinetics with explicit Cyp26 / Raldh2, quantitative reproduction of its hysteresis figures or of Dubrulle (2001) somite sizes, T1 transitions / epithelial rosette formation / apical constriction, the 90-degree Xenopus somite cell-block rotation, 3D epithelialisation mechanics, or explicit Delta-Notch intercellular delay coupling (Slots 022-023)." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 1976-cooke-clock-and-wavefront.py:1141-1149 — the FGF8 bead measurement is compared to a control ratio of 1.0 with a directional reference because Dubrulle et al. (2001) report no numerical somite-size ratio. Digitise the bead-side vs control somite sizes from Dubrulle (2001) or the simulated ratio from Goldbeter (2007) and use that as reference_value.",
            "remediation needed: 1976-cooke-clock-and-wavefront.py:125-132 — EXPECTED_SHA256 pins only the specimen and scout manifest; fgf_ra_vertex_reference.json and clock_and_wavefront_reference.json are recorded at runtime but not pinned, so the reference values used by measure_morphoeval() can drift silently. Pin both digests.",
            "remediation needed: 1976-cooke-clock-and-wavefront.py:136-148 and 266-336 — the FGF/RA toggle is a two-variable reduction with tuned normalised constants (alpha = 3, K = 1, n = 4, tau_FR = 12 min, k_dM = 0.0074/min) and Cyp26/Raldh2 lumped into two Hill terms. Implement the published Goldbeter et al. (2007) kinetics with explicit Cyp26 and Raldh2 and their parameter values, vendor the parameter table, and reproduce the paper's hysteresis figure quantitatively (bistable window position and width) instead of only locating M_lo = 0.53.",
            "remediation needed: 1976-cooke-clock-and-wavefront.py:150-161 and 800-825 — dLambda_cleft = 0.9 is tested only against 0, and the relaxation schedule (150 gradient steps per 40-min snapshot) has no physical time scale. Sweep dLambda over [0, 1.5] and show cleft angle and tortuosity are monotone, and calibrate the step/viscosity to a measured boundary-straightening time.",
            "remediation needed: 1976-cooke-clock-and-wavefront.py:765-876 — the vertex sheet has no T1 transitions, so the lattice zig-zag cleft can only rotate from 28.2 to 10.3 deg and its tortuosity floors at 1.03; there is no apical constriction or rosette term, so 'epithelial rosette cleft rotation' is reduced to cleft-edge reorientation. Add T1 edge swaps (edge length threshold) and a per-somite apical-constriction / rosette energy, and model the 90-degree Xenopus cell-block rotation (Afonin et al. 2006) as a measurable rotation of cell long axes.",
            "remediation needed: 1976-cooke-clock-and-wavefront.py:883-976 and datasets/clock_and_wavefront/clock_and_wavefront_reference.json:30-41 — the SEM specimen is a chick embryo in pixels without a scale bar, so S_obs = 48.47 px and the 7.9-deg cleft angle cannot be compared to S_sim in um or to Xenopus somites. Vendor a scale-calibrated Xenopus laevis somite micrograph (or add a scale for the chick SEM) and compare S_obs in um to S_sim.",
            "remediation needed: 1976-cooke-clock-and-wavefront.py:944-958 — the empirical cleft angle is a luminance-minimum line fit through 4-px bands over a 44-px row for 8 clefts, without uncertainty. Replace by an edge-traced boundary (e.g. Canny + Hough on the inter-somitic furrow) and report mean +/- sd for both rows." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.903"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (primary) + Claude Sonnet 5.5 High (independent second assessor)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "gemini-4-argon" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf orcid:0009-0007-4948-9192 ;
        foaf:homepage <https://deepmind.google> .
}

